  "summaryOfChange": "Re‑examined the notebook and recent day‑40 events, concluding that the dominant open anomaly is the near‑perfect three‑day lagged correlation between pendulum_lab and resonator_obs. The prior question was retained but sharpened to focus on this specific pairing. Probabilities were updated: the software‑pipeline hypothesis was raised from 0.67 to 0.60 to reflect stronger support from the exact 1.000 correlation and the lack of comparable effects elsewhere; scheduling bias and timestamp offset were added as new low‑probability alternatives; temperature, microseismic, and power‑grid hypotheses were demoted due to lack of supporting evidence and their failure to explain why only this pair is affected; a residual category was kept at 0.10. All probability values were renormalized to sum to 1."
}
